          "en": "is about those environment variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.49,
          "end": 8.75,
          "en": "And that's a very useful feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.75,
          "end": 12.2,
          "en": "since it allows us to use different values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.2,
          "end": 16.7,
          "en": "in parts of our code, during development and production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.7,
          "end": 21.08,
          "en": "And Next.js has built-in support for environment variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.08,
          "end": 23.403,
          "en": "Now to explore them, I actually wanna explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.403,
          "end": 25.75,
          "en": "another of concept first though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.75,
          "end": 28.85,
          "en": "We can configure Next.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.85,
          "end": 31.73,
          "en": "Up to this point, this Next.js project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.73,
          "end": 36.1,
          "en": "worked with all the default settings Next.js assumes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.1,
          "end": 40.37,
          "en": "And these are a sensible default, which often makes sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.37,
          "end": 43.12,
          "en": "But maybe you want to fine-tune them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.12,
          "end": 44.51,
          "en": "And you can do this by adding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.51,
          "end": 47.27,
          "en": "a special file to your project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.27,
          "end": 51.33,
          "en": "a next.config.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.33,
          "end": 54.94,
          "en": "This is a special file which has to be named like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.94,
          "end": 58.02,
          "en": "and which has to sit in your root project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.02,
          "end": 58.97,
          "en": "if you add it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.97,
          "end": 62.49,
          "en": "And it's a file, which exports a JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.49,
          "end": 66.01,
          "en": "with this Node.js export syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.01,
          "end": 67.92,
          "en": "If you never worked with Node.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.92,
          "end": 70.08,
          "en": "you might not know this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.08,
          "end": 74.05,
          "en": "This is in the end the equivalent to export default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.05,
          "end": 77.65,
          "en": "in front-end JavaScript so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.65,
          "end": 80.81,
          "en": "So we export such an object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.81,
          "end": 82.12,
          "en": "and that's now our object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.12,
          "end": 85.60300000000001,
          "en": "which allows you to set various configuration options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.47,
          "end": 88.76,
          "en": "Now, if you Google for next config",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.76,
          "end": 91.09,
          "en": "you'll find your official documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.09,
          "end": 92.9,
          "en": "on that config file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.9,
          "end": 95.45,
          "en": "And here you learn all about that file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.45,
          "end": 98.00999999999999,
          "en": "and what you can configure there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.00999999999999,
          "end": 102.08,
          "en": "You can configure a lot here, but for most of the settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.08,
          "end": 104.28999999999999,
          "en": "the defaults are fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.28999999999999,
          "end": 106.97,
          "en": "But you can, for example add environment variables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.97,
          "end": 108.57,
          "en": "something we'll do in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.57,
          "end": 110.21000000000001,
          "en": "You could add a basePath",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.21000000000001,
          "end": 114.1,
          "en": "if you're hosting your next website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.1,
          "end": 116.31,
          "en": "not on the root level of some domain,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.31,
          "end": 118.31,
          "en": "but in some nested path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.31,
          "end": 120.9,
          "en": "You can set up rewrites and redirects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.9,
          "end": 123.09,
          "en": "if you have some hard-coded redirects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.09,
          "end": 125.16,
          "en": "which should be taken into account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.16,
          "end": 129.38,
          "en": "when the application is deployed and much more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.38,
          "end": 132.45,
          "en": "You can inject your own Webpack configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 132.45,
          "end": 135.72,
          "en": "to really tap into that build process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.72,
          "end": 139.64,
          "en": "You can disable compression, it's enabled by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.64,
          "end": 142.31,
          "en": "but you can disable it if you don't wanna use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.31,
          "end": 144.06,
          "en": "for whatever reason.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.06,
          "end": 147.21,
          "en": "Compression will make your JavaScript files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.21,
          "end": 148.47,
          "en": "and so on smaller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.47,
          "end": 152.55,
          "en": "So you should enable it by default and much more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 152.55,
          "end": 154.74,
          "en": "So you see, there are a couple of things you can set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 154.74,
          "end": 159.62,
          "en": "but to be honest most of the settings will rarely be needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 159.62,
          "end": 162.6,
          "en": "And you will know when you need them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.6,
          "end": 165.63,
          "en": "The most helpful settings are probably redirects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165.63,
          "end": 168.34,
          "en": "and custom headers and environment variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.34,
          "end": 170.28,
          "en": "and the basePath.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.28,
          "end": 172.93,
          "en": "For this project though, we need no rewrites.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 172.93,
          "end": 175.11,
          "en": "We don't need to change the basePath.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 175.11,
          "end": 177.2,
          "en": "We don't need any custom headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 177.2,
          "end": 180.56,
          "en": "but we will explore environment variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 180.56,
          "end": 185.22,
          "en": "And the idea really is that in our API route here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.22,
          "end": 188.82,
          "en": "we swap out some of these values here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.82,
          "end": 192.33,
          "en": "from this connection string for dynamic values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 192.33,
          "end": 196.26,
          "en": "which can then differ between development and production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 196.26,
          "end": 199.4,
          "en": "So that we can have a development database connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 199.4,
          "end": 201.39,
          "en": "and a production database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 201.39,
          "end": 205.55,
          "en": "And we don't delete or manipulate production data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 205.55,
          "end": 208.38,
          "en": "with our development tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 208.38,
          "end": 212.31,
          "en": "And to make that work, I'll go to that next config file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 212.31,
          "end": 214.93,
          "en": "and add the env key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 214.93,
          "end": 218.56,
          "en": "That's also what you see in the official docs here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 218.56,
          "end": 222.67000000000002,
          "en": "This allows you to set up key value pairs of your choices",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.67000000000002,
          "end": 227.22,
          "en": "and you will then be able to use your keys in your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.22,
          "end": 232.22,
          "en": "both in the API routes, as well as in any other component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.04,
          "end": 236.02,
          "en": "So you can use your environment variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.02,
          "end": 238.023,
          "en": "anywhere in your code base.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.27,
          "end": 243.94,
          "en": "So here all of the setup a couple of environment variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.94,
          "end": 248.67,
          "en": "and I'll start with MongoDB username.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 248.67,
          "end": 250.88,
          "en": "Now how you named that variable is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 250.88,
          "end": 254.43,
          "en": "but I'll name it like this and set this to Maximilian.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 254.43,
          "end": 259.43,
          "en": "Then add the MongoDB password and set this to the password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 259.93,
          "end": 264.41,
          "en": "I have here in my connection string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 265.98,
          "end": 269.493,
          "en": "then I'll add the MongoDB cluster name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 270.4,
          "end": 275.4,
          "en": "And here I will use this cluster zero thing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.22,
          "end": 279.47,
          "en": "so that if I had multiple clusters in my account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 279.47,
          "end": 282.94,
          "en": "I can use different clusters for different environments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 282.94,
          "end": 284.92,
          "en": "So I'll add this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 284.92,
          "end": 289.587,
          "en": "And then I'll also add the MongoDB database key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 291.2,
          "end": 293.4,
          "en": "And here, I wanna grab that database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.4,
          "end": 298.4,
          "en": "to which I'm connecting my-site and set this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 298.89,
          "end": 301.04,
          "en": "Now you might be wondering why I'm doing this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.04,
          "end": 302.88,
          "en": "What's the benefit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 302.88,
          "end": 307.56,
          "en": "The benefit is that now we can tap into those values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.56,
          "end": 309.15,
          "en": "We'll do that in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 309.15,
          "end": 311.73,
          "en": "And when we then deploy our application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.73,
          "end": 314.33,
          "en": "we can override these values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 314.33,
          "end": 316.12,
          "en": "and you'll see how we can override them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 316.12,
          "end": 319,
          "en": "in a couple of minutes, once we deploy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319,
          "end": 321.01,
          "en": "And therefore we now need to switch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.01,
          "end": 323.81,
          "en": "to using environment variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 323.81,
          "end": 325.81,
          "en": "So back in the API route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 325.81,
          "end": 330.81,
          "en": "I'll now set up my connection string here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 331.33,
          "end": 333.25,
          "en": "in a separate constant simply to make it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 333.25,
          "end": 334.89,
          "en": "a bit easier to work with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 334.89,
          "end": 337.21,
          "en": "And I'll set up a template literal here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 337.21,
          "end": 341.92,
          "en": "because now I need to mix hard-coded and dynamic values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 341.92,
          "end": 346.92,
          "en": "And I'll still start with that MongoDB plus SRV part here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 347.62,
          "end": 349.33,
          "en": "but then after the two slashes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 349.33,
          "end": 354.23,
          "en": "I wanna inject the value from my environment variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 354.23,
          "end": 358.123,
          "en": "from that MongoDB username environment variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 359.65,
          "end": 361.6,
          "en": "And here we see in the official docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 361.6,
          "end": 363.86,
          "en": "that we get access to those values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 363.86,
          "end": 368.22,
          "en": "by tapping into the global process variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 368.22,
          "end": 372.53,
          "en": "which is exposed by Node.js, then dote env",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 372.53,
          "end": 375.47,
          "en": "and then into the key name of our choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 375.47,
          "end": 378.06,
          "en": "Now this placeholder will be replaced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 378.06,
          "end": 381.57,
          "en": "with the concrete value during the build process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 381.57,
          "end": 383.04,
          "en": "That's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 383.04,
          "end": 385.673,
          "en": "So this will not be resolved to dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 385.673,
          "end": 387.81,
          "en": "after we built the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 387.81,
          "end": 391.59,
          "en": "but it will be swapped out during the build process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 391.59,
          "end": 393.27,
          "en": "And that allows us to replace it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 393.27,
          "end": 395.58,
          "en": "with our environment variable value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 395.58,
          "end": 397.89,
          "en": "And it allows us to use different values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 397.89,
          "end": 401.55,
          "en": "for building, for production, then during development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 401.55,
          "end": 404.15999999999997,
          "en": "But again, we're going to see this in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 404.15999999999997,
          "end": 407.6,
          "en": "So they are for now in contact.js here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 407.6,
          "end": 411.51,
          "en": "I now want to use process.env.mongodb username here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 415.15,
          "end": 418.53,
          "en": "Then we have a colon here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 418.53,
          "end": 421.68,
          "en": "So this is hard-coded and there after the password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 421.68,
          "end": 425.283,
          "en": "which we get from process.env.mongodb_password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
